  "question": {
    "text": "The water is filled up to a height of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> in a tank having vertical sidewalls. A hole is made in one of the walls at a depth&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math> below the water level. The value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math> for which the emerging stream of water strikes the ground at the maximum range is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0067_68924071f571.png\" style=\"width: 386px; height: 204px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></msqrt><mo>&#215;</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#160;</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi></math></p><p>For maximum <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p>"
  }
